A||||3||Slammed Fiero||Rode in a 425hp eagle Talon||||1||
Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||09-05-2001||11:11 PM||||Dammm...<P>12.3 in the 1/4. Our local sports car club , held a lapping night at Shannonville motorsport park , the course is about 3.8kms long. On the long straight we were hitting 120mph. The car pulled like a freight train in every gear. The car has been featured in Turbo , turned a 12.3 on street tires with No NOS. it handeled really well , but the weight of the car was a  little too much for the brakes and we baked them after a few laps.<P>Also got a few laps in a very well prepared Mr2 SC , believe it or not he was nearly as fast around the track as the Talon , what he lost in the straights , gained in the corners.<P>Also got a ride in a well prepped 93 240. Stock motor , but the brakes are from a 300zx and the car has a few suspension mods. This seemd like the most stable car of the bunch I rode in.<P>Unfortunatley due to "corded" rear tires I was unable to run , but I picked upa  set of real pirelli P zero's for free.<P>There was also a full race fiero there , but the owner was working out some glitches.<P>I completed (Finally) my brake conversion 11.25". What a difference , nothing short of amazing on hoe the car stops now. Plus looking at 17" wheels with the originally rotors looked kinda goofy (sorry to anyone)<P><BR>Tomorrow ...Getting the nOS filled<P>Giddy Up. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||09-05-2001||11:13 PM||||hey jonathan, has nothing to do with the talon but email me, about my short shifter||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||09-05-2001||11:19 PM||||I really like those 240's.  My friend is going to buy one for a project car, drop in an SR20DET motor, around 220 Hp.  He said the swap is very easy and cheap, for around 12 grand he can get everything done, on a low mileage car.  <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000003||artherd||09-06-2001||05:28 PM||||Hi Jonathan, didja manage to get another set of the "c" spec Pirellis?  Northstar car is getting 'zeros wether she likes it or not, grin.<P>Coolness on the brakes, I think I might just try and adapt some Big Reds, but oh the $ just starts piling up :S)<P>Hopefully I'll have the car ready by the time Sears Point opens back up here.<P>425hp with no NO2?!? Jeeeesus  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I wonder how many AWDs he's gone through? (I always wonder about the drivetrains you see on those little '500hp' insanely turbo race gas civics, what do they DO? <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>Edited because I spelled your name wrong, doh!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">   <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||3
